# Started by systemd when paw-user-erasure.service fails (OnFailure=).
# The run already recorded each user it could not erase in audit_events whenever
# the database accepted it (action auth.user.erase, decision deny, the reason)
# and wrote the user ids and reasons to the journal
# (journalctl -u paw-user-erasure.service). Those users stay pending deletion,
# without access, past their 30 days: REQUIREMENTS.md asks that the Owner hears
# of it.
# A run also fails, from the FIRST day of a deletion, for every pending-deletion
# user whose own GitHub / SSH credentials are not confirmed revoked (action
# auth.user.credentials, decision deny, reason credentials_pending; the journal
# says "ACTION REQUIRED"): revoke them, then confirm with --credentials-revoked.
#
# Replace ExecStart with the notification channel of your deployment (mail, a
# chat webhook, ...) if you have one; keep credentials of that channel out of
# this file.

[Unit]
Description=Report a failed user erasure run of the Personal AI Workspace

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/bin/systemd-cat --identifier=paw-user-erasure --priority=crit /bin/echo "user erasure FAILED: see journalctl -u paw-user-erasure.service and audit_events (decision deny). action auth.user.erase: the users named are past their 30 days and not erased. action auth.user.credentials (credentials_pending, from the first day of a deletion): revoke those users' GitHub / SSH credentials, then run with --credentials-revoked."
ExecStart=/usr/bin/wall "Personal AI Workspace: user erasure FAILED (journalctl -u paw-user-erasure.service)."
